# Team Tactics: "Teamwork 1 ... If this spell was cast using teamwork, that creature also gains trample until end of turn." On turn 3
# Bot1 taps one Memnite (power 1, exactly the total needed) to pay and gives the other double strike and trample. It attacks and is
# blocked by Bot2's Crimson Kobolds (0/1): the first-strike damage of 1 kills the blocker, and the regular damage of 1 tramples over
# to Bot2 (CR 702.4b, 702.19b) - without trample a creature blocked by nothing now would deal none - so Bot2 is at 19.

[Bot1 Deck]
Team Tactics
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Memnite
Memnite
Crimson Kobolds
Island
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Crimson Kobolds
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Crimson Kobolds.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Crimson Kobolds.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Team Tactics.Cast
Bot1.Modes(Teamwork 1)
Bot1.Target(Memnite#1)
! Bot1.Choose(Crimson Kobolds)
Bot1.Choose(Memnite#2)
? Bot1.Mana =
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Memnite#2.Tapped = true
? Bot1.Battlefield.Memnite#1.Keywords = DoubleStrike; Trample
[T3 Bot1.DeclareAttackers]
Bot1.Attack(Memnite#1 > Bot2)
Bot2.Block(Crimson Kobolds > Memnite#1)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 19
Bot2.Graveyard = Crimson Kobolds
Bot1.Battlefield.Memnite#1.Damage = 0
